/**
 * The `contain` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property indicates that an
 * element and its contents are, as much as possible, independent from the rest of the document
 * tree. Containment enables isolating a subsection of the DOM, providing performance benefits by
 * limiting calculations of layout, style, paint, size, or any combination to a DOM subtree rather
 * than the entire page. Containment can also be used to scope CSS counters and quotes.
 *
 * Initial: none. Inherited: no.
 * Percentages: not accepted.
 *
 * Grammar: none | strict | content | [ [size | inline-size] || layout || style || paint ]
 *
 * Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-contain-2/#propdef-contain
